WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.202
President Biden was actually on Air Force

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:02.902
One traveling

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.037
from Syracuse, New York,

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.638
to Hagerstown, Maryland,

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.706
when the military

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.974
undertook this operation

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.276
to take down that Chinese spy balloon.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.645
President Biden spoke to reporters

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.913
just in the last hour

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:14.581
where he tried

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.716
to clearly lay out the timeline

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.785
of when he gave that order, saying

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.787
he told his military officials

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.022
he wanted to shoot down

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.157
that plane as soon as possible.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.791
Take a listen to

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.060
what the president had to say.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.229
On Wednesday.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.164
When I was briefed on the balloon,

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.132
I went to the Pentagon

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.234
to shoot it down on Wednesday

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.069
as soon as possible.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.204
They decided without doing damage

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.474
to anyone on the ground and decided

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.442
that the best time to do

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:44.544
that was to look out over water

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.080
outside of debris that are within 12 mile

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.649
limit They successfully took it down.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.285
And I want to compliment our aviators

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.186
who did it.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.655
And we'll have more to report on this

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:56.723
a little later.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:57.257
Thank you.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:57.724
This is

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.927
what they say about our message to China.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.263
You were saying the recommendation

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.497
from here was from your national.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.632
I told them to shoot it

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.833
down on Wednesday.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.101
I want to make a recommendation.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.569
They said to me, let's wait for

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.904
the safest place to do it.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.340
So the president quite emphatic there

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.041
that he did

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.643
give that order on Wednesday

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:17.077
of course,

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.546
he had been facing a slew of criticism

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.714
from Republicans up on Capitol Hill

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.349
who had slammed the president

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.085
for not taking action sooner.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.320
We've heard from Republicans today

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.388
praising the decision

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.423
to shoot down that balloon,

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.058
but they did say that they wish

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:32.959
that he had taken

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.227
these steps much sooner.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.962
Of course, there have also been Democrats

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.163
who have major questions

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:37.997
for the White House

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.099
about how exactly

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.467
this has all played out.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.568
Senator Mark Warner,

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.202
the head

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:42.669
of the Senate

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:43.570
Intelligence Committee,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.437
earlier in the week,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.505
said that China

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.339
itself wouldn't

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.540
have allowed a balloon like this

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.075
to fly over their heartland.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.144
We know that Senator Jon Tester,

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.713
who is the chair of a subcommittee

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:54.581
for Appropriations

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:55.648
that deals with defense,

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.516
he has said

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.718
that he wants to hold hearings

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.353
relating to this matter.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.821
But certainly the president has faced

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.256
a lot of political pressure.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.891
Of course, I will note he was asked there

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.693
what kind of message this sends to China.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.461
He did not answer that question.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.662
But this certainly serves

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.231
as a major tension point

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.632
in that relationship with China.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:14.200
Well, I

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.401
think the United States has sent

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.337
that message our lead signs.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.171
Thank you very much.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:18.404
With me

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.672
now on the phone is CNN's chief

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.473
national security

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.342
correspondent, Jim Sciutto.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.977
Jim, to that point,

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.479
I mean, I guess we're reaching a new,

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.915
I guess, moment in the relationship,

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:29.883
tense relationship

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.618
between the United States and China.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.287
And President Biden making it very clear

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:35.889
on Wednesday

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:38.525
he wanted to shoot this thing down.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.993
It's a critical moment, Jim,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.994
in the relationship

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.462
between two superpowers,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.397
which was already tense

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.999
and is now more tense.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.333
Of course, the first hostile

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.368
act, China

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.202
floating

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.670
this highly capable surveillance

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.205
balloon over the continental U.S.,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.474
including overflying several

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.576
sensitive installations.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.144
And now a U.S.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.345
president making a decision

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.713
to to acquire

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.149
weapons, fire a missile from an F 22 fire

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:03.716
fighter jet

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.619
to destroy that surveillance balloon,

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.621
but also critically take it down in U.S.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.556
territorial waters

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.257
off the coast of South Carolina

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.959
with ships on the surface

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.094
there as we're told

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.229
that going to make an attempt

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.198
at least to collect

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:18.831
what it can

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.265
from here,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.133
that they can

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.334
further learn

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.336
exactly what Chinese capabilities are.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.504
I think it's also critical

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.339
to note to Jim,

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.541
as he was saying, that the U.S.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.143
says they were able to block

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.377
the surveillance balloons, ability

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.713
to gather intelligence over the U.S.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.114
while at the same time, in effect,

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.382
turning the tables

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.052
to gather intelligence on their planes

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.386
capabilities. That's critical.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.021
But I think big picture,

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.223
this is a tense moment.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.724
It was already tense.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:45.391
We had a U.S.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.593
Air Force general

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.427
within the last week

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:50.530
or so mourning his forces

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.264
under his command

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.899
to be prepared for the prospect of war

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.934
with China soon to be 20, 25.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.270
That's not the consensus assessment

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.304
from the U.S.,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.839
but it's not far off

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.774
from the urgency that U.S.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.776
officials feel about the prospects

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.011
for escalation

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.412
with China in the coming years.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.482
And now you have a very tangible instance

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.452
of that with the missiles fired

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.488
in anger or in response to a Chinese

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.323
provocation, a tense time.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.359
Absolutely.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:19.692
We might

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.026
and we

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.995
might see more provocations to come.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.229
Jim Sciutto,

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.631
thanks for that Expertize, as always.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.298
We appreciate it.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:26.866
I want to go now to CNN's Tom Foreman

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.201
for more on the spy balloon.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.103
He's been watching this all day.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.272
Tom, a very dramatic conclusion

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.374
to what has been a tense few days over

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.109
the United States with this balloon

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.510
making its way across the country.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.311
Yeah, we're actually coming up

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.712
on three full days of this

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.847
being part of the game here.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.415
It's believed that it took off from China

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.283
here, came up over

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.418
the Aleutian Islands past Alaska,

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.320
Canada down this way,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.389
and then ended up down in here.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.959
That would be roughly an 8500 mile

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.094
trip or a third of the distance

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.062
around the world.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:56.896
Let's look at what it came

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.698
over, though, on the way here

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.767
when we had these spottings here,

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.869
we it gave us an idea of the path

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.003
it was following through

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.438
the United States here

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.072
as these reports

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.540
that maybe it was guided to some degree.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.442
But this also matches up pretty well

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:09.809
with what

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:10.777
the jet stream would do

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.145
with any balloon out there.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.413
What did it pass over?

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.815
Close to a dozen nuclear facilities,

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.617
missile facilities,

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.152
somewhere around five or six

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.787
large military facilities

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:21.521
along the way here.

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:22.822
And, of course, some fairly big towns.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.224
It got reasonably close to Kansas City,

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.361
Saint Louis, Nashville and some others

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.863
before coming in to its its finish

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.398
here at the end.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.499
Oren said a moment ago

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.434
something very interesting

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:34.967
when you pair it

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.703
with what Jim was saying there.

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.438
They said that this is in 47

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:39.605
feet of water.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.741
We had already looked at the ocean shelf

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:42.642
out here

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.877
up to about 35 miles before you go out.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.146
It can go up to 600, 700 feet.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.748
So 15, 47 feet.

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:51.617
That is a very precise excellent

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.853
depth for them to recover it in.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.954
It also means they know

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.422
precisely where it came down,

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.391
that it didn't get lost in the fall.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.292
And they're out there looking for it.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.627
They know where it is really important.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:03.162
The question now is

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.931
what are they going to find?

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:05.798
One of the questions

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.333
that military analysts will have about

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:08.401
this is,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.669
was the information

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.037
that was being collected,

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:11.437
the stuff

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.772
they couldn't block or whatever

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.273
they were trying to block,

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.642
was that native to this hardware?

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:18.845
Did it live here in some fashion

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.179
on some kind of drive

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:20.847
some kind of chip,

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:21.514
some sort of something?

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.950
Or was it being streamed to China?

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.753
And is all the memory here empty?

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.154
Does it mean it's useless?

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:29.021
Even if you don't have that,

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.523
you'd at least have the hardware

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:30.857
to give you

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.892
some idea of what it was supposed to do

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:33.860
along the way,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.293
some of what

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.895
it might have been looking at.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.563
Those are key things they have to look at

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:39.232
when they look through this technology.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.400
Once they're able to fish it

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.567
out of the water,

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.436
which they hope they can do down here.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:44.771
And that has not been damaged

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:46.839
too terribly in the fall Jim.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:47.273
All right.

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:47.673
Tom Ford,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.608
we know the Pentagon wants

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:49.108
to get its hands

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.843
on that balloon and all of the equipment

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:51.344
coming with it. Tom, thanks so much.

